  "analysis": "Final round. Kept backbone (R2 C2, mAP 0.625): 24/13/13 inclusion-heavy, same_class, 0.3-0.7, max_overlap 0.15. Miss analysis shows a consistent cross-class signal: missed instances are systematically smaller than train medians (inclusion 34 vs 90px, patches 49 vs 85px, scratches 40 vs 73px) and low-tertile recall is worst for inclusion (0.219, n=146). Proven: small scale, same_class, inclusion-heavy. Refuted: any_class backgrounds, scratch mid-scale 0.5-1.0. Untested: source-size bias and appearance-matched source selection. All 3 candidates keep the proven backbone and change one factor each: (1) inclusion pastes restricted to the small vertical streak/blob sources that visually match the missed inclusions (excluding the large irregular 99); (2) the missing 2x2 cell — inclusion 0.3-0.5 (27-45px, tightest match to the 34px missed band) combined with the proven heavy allocation; (3) prefer_small source weighting for patches and scratches to push their pastes into the missed size band. Control (repeat of kept plan) is the baseline to beat.",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "hypothesis": "Missed inclusions (median 34px, 146/179 in low tertile) are small vertical dark streaks/blobs; the large irregular source 99 is a poor match. Restricting inclusion pastes to the 8 small/vertical sources (11, 150, 50, 268, 277, 100, 106, 131) at the proven 0.3-0.7 scale should lift inclusion AP50 above ~0.40 and mAP above 0.625; if inclusion AP stays ~0.38, appearance-matched source selection is not the lever.",
      "allocation": {"inclusion": 24, "patches": 13, "scratches": 13},
      "params": {
        "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [11, 150, 50, 268, 277, 100, 106, 131]},
        "patches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
      }
    },
    {
      "hypothesis": "R2 tested 0.3-0.5 with balanced allocation (0.6205) and 0.3-0.7 with heavy allocation (0.625) separately; the missing cell is 0.3-0.5 + heavy. Since missed inclusions center at ~34px (0.3-0.5 of ~90px sources = 27-45px), tightening the inclusion scale band while keeping the proven 24/13/13 allocation should raise inclusion AP50 toward 0.40+; if it merely ties the control, 0.3-0.7 was already the sweet spot and scale is not the remaining inclusion lever.",
      "allocation": {"inclusion": 24, "patches": 13, "scratches": 13},
      "params": {
        "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.5, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "patches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
      }
    },
    {
      "hypothesis": "Missed patches (49px vs 85px train median) and scratches (40px vs 73px) are also systematically smaller than what uniform-source pastes produce, so biasing both classes toward smaller sources (prefer_small) at the proven 0.3-0.7 scale should improve their low-tertile recall and lift patches/scratches AP50 above 0.785/0.705 without touching the proven inclusion recipe; if either class drops by >0.03, small-source bias is harmful and uniform weighting stays.",
      "allocation": {"inclusion": 24, "patches": 13, "scratches": 13},
      "params": {
        "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "patches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
      }
    }
  ]
}

